## Negative-test seam proof

- Programmatic mode rejection starts from a valid fresh `Default()` and mutates only mode.
- The YAML whitespace case uses `mode: "inline "`, so yaml.v3 preserves the invalid trailing byte.
- Case variants and primary/fallback errors use independent literal expectations naming `seat["opus"].mode` and `seat["opus"].invocation_fallbacks[0].mode`; an earlier shape error cannot satisfy them.
- Tests clone the fallback slice before mutation, avoiding shared backing-array assumptions.

## Identifier compatibility audit

- `validateStageName` has exactly one caller. That caller rejects blank/whitespace stage names before applying the shared predicate, so the helper's non-empty rule cannot newly reject an optional value.
- Named runners only call the shared predicate inside `if r.Name != ""`; unnamed command runners retain their existing path.
- Registry preserves its explicit empty-key error before the shared predicate.
- `runmanifest.IsValidIdentifier` already rejected empty and remains the exported wrapper; its existing literal predicate and run-ID tests pass unchanged.

